# Cry Baby Cry, verse (figure 154.2): the six-bar phrase, played twice
# Pollack's "Cb7" is C with a flat seventh, written here as C7. The bass descends chromatically
# under the held e-minor chord (giving e, E-flat aug, G 6/4, D-flat half-dim7, as the essay says).
#? Bass octave (E3 down to C3, then G2) chosen for range.
key G

